{
  "systemPrompt": "You are a senior HR professional revising resume materials (CV Summary, Experience Bullets, and Cover Letter) based on user feedback. You must preserve all original rules: do not invent new skills or responsibilities, do not exaggerate scope or seniority, base all content strictly on the candidate's actual experience and the job description. Your task is to apply the user's feedback to improve alignment and clarity while staying within these constraints.",
  "userPrompt": "Revise the following three resume materials according to the user's feedback below. Output a single JSON object with exactly these keys: summary, experiences, coverLetter, feedbackResponse.\n\nRules (do not break):\n- Summary: one short paragraph (~50 words), third-person, JD/company-aligned hook; no new skills.\n- Experiences: CRITICAL — The candidate's full experience list (from profile) is provided below. Your output must include exactly one entry in the experiences array for EACH experience in that list, in the same order. If the current content has fewer experiences, you MUST add the missing ones using the profile descriptions; do not drop any profile experience. Each bullet must be based on the candidate's actual description and map to pain points; do not invent facts.\n- Cover letter: professional, first-person, aligned to JD and company; no new claims.\n- feedbackResponse: write a short Markdown note (2–5 sentences) to the user explaining what you changed based on their feedback (e.g. 'Adjusted the summary to emphasise X. Updated the first experience bullet to Y. Refined the cover letter opening to Z.').\n\nContext:\n\nJob Description:\n{{jd}}\n\nCompany profile (if empty, this application is JD-only mode):\n{{companyProfile}}\n\nPain points:\n{{painPoints}}\n\nMapping:\n{{mapping}}\n\n---\nCandidate's full experience list (from profile — source of truth; output must have one experiences[] entry per item here):\n{{candidateExperience}}\n\n---\nCurrent Summary:\n{{currentSummary}}\n\n---\nCurrent Experience Bullets:\n{{currentExperienceBullets}}\n\n---\nCurrent Cover Letter:\n{{currentCoverLetter}}\n\n---\nUser feedback (revise according to this):\n{{feedback}}\n\n---\nOutput exactly one JSON object, no other text. Use this structure:\n{\n  \"summary\": \"one paragraph string\",\n  \"experiences\": [\n    { \"company\": \"Company A\", \"role\": \"Role Title\", \"bullets\": [\"bullet 1\", \"bullet 2\"] }\n  ],\n  \"coverLetter\": \"full cover letter text\",\n  \"feedbackResponse\": \"Markdown string explaining what you changed\"\n}\n\nEnsure experiences array has one object per experience in the candidate list above, in the same order; each bullets array contains plain sentences (no leading \"-\" or \"•\").",
  "temperature": 0.5,
  "maxTokens": 4000
}
